    "question": "What man, also known as mi Sde-Or, created a military self-defense system developed for the Israel Defense Forces?",
    "gold_answer": "Emrich \"Imi\" Lichtenfeld",
    "gold_titles": [
      "Imi Lichtenfeld",
      "Krav Maga"
    ],
    "system_answer": "The man also known as **Imi Sde-Or** is **Imi Lichtenfeld** (born Emrich Lichtenfeld), a Hungarian-born Israeli martial artist [1]. He created the military self-defense system known as **Krav Maga** [1][2].\n\nLichtenfeld developed Krav Maga for the Israel Defense Forces (IDF) and Israeli security forces (including Shin Bet and Mossad) [2]. The system was derived from his training as a boxer and wrestler, as well as his practical street-fighting experience defending the Jewish quarter against fascist groups in Bratislava during the late 1930s [2]. Following his migration to Israel, he began providing combat training in the late 1940s to the forces that would eventually become the IDF [2]. The name \"Imi Sde-Or\" is the Hebrew calque of his original surname, Lichtenfeld [1].",
    "retrieved_titles": [
      "Imi Lichtenfeld",
      "Krav Maga",
      "Bruce Lee",
      "Tommy Chang (martial artist)"
    ],
    "answer_correct": false,
